ngular mathematical promenade (https://perso.ens-lyon.fr/ghys/reviews/Munoz.pdf)\nciteturn681search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.0 years ago; Crawled: 5.9 years ago; A singular mathematical promenade ... Notions of combinatorics, discrete mathematics (like the analysis of trees), algebra (operads), algebraic geometry (resolution of curve singularities, complex singularities), are explained in an enlightening way, changing mathematical rigour for clarifying drawings in a wise choice. ... Book details panel with the same descriptive blurb, and labeled fields: Author: Étienne Ghys; Publisher: ENS Editions; Published: 2017; ISBN: 978-2-84788-939-0; Price: 27 euros; Pages: 302; link: http://www.ens-lyon.fr/editions/catalogue\nThe author has done good work in accounting on the history of some very classical notions (just to name a few, the fundamental theorem of algebra, or the theory of Puiseux series, the linking number of knots, but there are very many), and he has made a very loable effort (and very successful indeed!) to transmitting this in a friendly, amusing and rigorous manner. Notions of combinatorics, discrete mathematics (like the analysis of trees), algebra (operads), algebraic geometry (resolution of curve singularities, complex singularities), are explained in an enlightening way, changing mathematical rigour for clarifying drawings in a wise choice.\n\nThe layout of the book is also impressive: it contains many nice photographs, pictures and drawings, also scans of manuscripts, historial bibliographic references, references of papers and books on mathematical concepts, clarifying remarks, all distributed in a column at the right of the page (so that one has the information immediately available). The text contains many historical quotations in different languages, with translations, and interesting analysis of the mathematics of our \"classics\" (Newton, Gauss, Hipparchus, are among hundreds of other names mentioned along the text).\n\nOne last word. The book is available for free at the arxiv: https://arxiv.org/ftp/arxiv/papers/1612/1612.06373.pdf  \nIt is published with a price of 27 euros. Just let me say that, after reading the copy of my library for writing this review, I will buy a personal copy for myself. I really enjoyed it!\n\nReviewer: Vicente Munoz  \nAffiliation: Universidad Complutense de Madrid\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nBook details panel with the same descriptive blurb, and labeled fields: Author: Étienne Ghys; Publisher: ENS Editions; Published: 2017; ISBN: 978-2-84788-939-0; Price: 27 euros; Pages: 302; link: http://www.ens-lyon.fr/editions/catalogue\n</visual_element>\n\n<visual_element id=\"e2\">\nCategorisation panel listing three categories: Algebraic And Complex Geometry; History Of Mathematics; Mathematics Education And Popularization Of Mathematics\n</visual_element>\n\n<visual_element id=\"e3\">\nFooter line with user/date metadata: Submitted by Vicente Munoz | 14 / Feb / 2018\n</visual_element>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCombinatorial and Asymptotic Methods of Algebra Non-Associative Structures (https://store.fmi.uni-sofia.bg/fmi/algebra/drensky/algebra_vi.pdf)\nciteturn681search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 25.2 years ago; Crawled: 19.2 years ago; (1989): Gröbner bases in noncommutative algebras. ... (1986): Basic notions of algebra.\nShafarevich, I.R. (1972): Foundations of Algebraic Geometry. Moscow, Nauka. English  \ntransl.: Berlin-Heidelberg-New York, Springer-Verlag 1974. Zbl. 258.14001. 2nd ed.  \n(1988). Zbl. 675.14001\n\nShafarevich, I.R. (1986): Basic notions of algebra. Itogi Nauk Tekh., Ser. Sovrem. Probl.  \nMat., Fundam. Napravleniya 11, 290 p. English transl. in: Encyclopaedia of Mathemati-  \ncal Sciences 11, Berlin-Heidelberg-New York, Springer-Verlag 1990. Zbl. 655.00002, Zbl.  \n711.16001--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThis book is dedicated to my Mother and